            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0234" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Executive Agreement Series No. 55</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of External Affairs of the Union of South
                        Africa (Hertzog) to the American Minister
                        in the Union of South Africa (Totten)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pretoria</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-09-20">20 September,
                        1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to refer to your letter
                    No. 167 of the 17th March last regarding the proposed arrangement between the
                    Union of South Africa and the United States of America providing for the
                    issuance by each country of licences to Nationals of the other country
                    authorizing <pb facs="0235" n="131" xml:id="pg131"/> them to pilot civil
                    aircraft, and to inform you that His Majesty’s Government in the Union of South
                    Africa are in accord with the terms of the arrangement which is, word for word
                    as follows:— <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>[Here follows text of the arrangement as given in note No. 167, March 17,
                            printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.]</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>It is further agreed that the arrangement will be operative as from the date of
                    this note.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. M. Hertzog</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
